From 12170942bad9aa718b8a1d8a3052637950d925a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:05:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 156/206] analyze_snapshot: stop deduplicating self_pp's
 pool_indices (theirs does not)

Measured over hello+prog, the two independent fixtures, against their 9619
self_pp element slots:

  dedup ON   ours 8263 slots, 1356 missing, 462 functions not ordered-equal
  dedup OFF  ours 9617 slots,    2 missing,   2 functions not ordered-equal

diff_units.sh shorebird 41344 -> 39425. Their collector plainly does not
deduplicate pool references, so the default flips to 0.

This is not a clean reproduction: prog fn#1580 and fn#1633 each emit 14 slots
where theirs emits 15, both short of pool index 1332. self_pp is ordered-equal
on 4594/4596 functions, not 4596/4596, and the comment above the switch says so.

Reprintable by spikes/shorebird_linkinfo_oracle/nc3_f67_pool_seen_multiset.sh
(default-agnostic; four one-slot perturbation controls; binary sha256 restore
proof).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_api_impl.cc b/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_api_impl.cc
index abe7627554a..493810e0bce 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_api_impl.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_api_impl.cc
@@ -1082,10 +1082,25 @@ static constexpr intptr_t kNoSelector = -1;
 // default-agnostic: it reads whichever value is committed, measures it, flips,
 // measures again, restores and proves the binary comes back byte for byte.
 //
+// Measured (hello+prog, the two independent fixtures; theirs = 9619 self_pp
+// element slots):
+//   dedup ON  ours 8263 slots, 1356 missing, 462 functions not ordered-equal
+//   dedup OFF ours 9617 slots,    2 missing,   2 functions not ordered-equal
+// diff_units.sh shorebird went 41344 -> 39425 with the dedup off. Theirs plainly
+// does not deduplicate, so neither do we: the default is 0.
+//
+// ⚠️ This is NOT the clean reproduction F66 got on subgraph_selectors. Two prog
+// functions still come up one slot short -- index_in_entries 1580 and 1633,
+// ours 14 slots against their 15, both missing pool index 1332 -- so the
+// undeduped self_pp is ordered-equal on 4594 of 4596 functions and NOT on all
+// of them. The honest reading therefore stays "the values match and the order
+// matches everywhere we can see except at those two sites", not "our walk is
+// theirs". Those two functions are the whole remaining self_pp evidence debt.
+//
 // 1 = dedup ON (the historical behaviour). 0 = emit every pool reference the
 // classifier fires on, in walk order.
 #ifndef F67_POOL_SEEN_DEDUP
-#define F67_POOL_SEEN_DEDUP 1
+#define F67_POOL_SEEN_DEDUP 0
 #endif
 
 // `add lr, x0, x17` makes the row index (origin + x17), so whatever was
